# =============================================================================
# VirtualPyTest — "Run Command on Hosts" admin feature (OPT-IN, OFF BY DEFAULT)
# =============================================================================
#
# Lets the backend_host service user (vpt_user) run ANY command as root
# without a password, so admin-authored maintenance scripts submitted through
# the admin-only "Settings > Run Command" page work (e.g. fleet-wide
# permission/config/service changes).
#
# This is intentionally broad: the feature's whole purpose is arbitrary
# privileged maintenance, and "arbitrary" cannot be enumerated into command
# patterns. Installing this file effectively makes vpt_user root-equivalent
# on this host.
#
# The privileged path is NOT gated by sudoers scope — it is gated by:
#   * admin JWT / role enforcement on backend_server
#     (@require_user_auth + @require_role('admin') on /server/system/runCommandOnHost)
#   * X-API-Key between backend_server and backend_host
#   * the frontend admin-only ProtectedRoute
#
# Kept as a SEPARATE drop-in (not merged into /etc/sudoers.d/virtualpytest) so
# an operator can instantly disable the privileged path with a single command
# without touching the curated rules:
#
#     sudo rm /etc/sudoers.d/run-command
#
# Install on a host:
#     sudo install -o root -g root -m 0440 \
#         /opt/virtualpytest/setup/local/linux/backend_host/sudoers.d/run-command \
#         /etc/sudoers.d/run-command
#     sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/run-command
# =============================================================================

# SETENV is required so callers can use `sudo -E` to preserve env vars
# (e.g. BluetoothRemoteController._run_script invokes start.sh / resume.sh
# as `sudo -n -E <path>`, passing ADAPTER_HCI / BLE_TYPE via env). Without
# SETENV on this broad rule, sudo evaluates run-command as the last-matching
# rule for /opt/.../start.sh, rejects -E, and fails with "a password is
# required" — which is what host3 hit during BLE pairing.
vpt_user ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: SETENV: ALL
